# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# FFmpeg's default branch is master, not main -- kb-update must pass --ref explicitly, never assume main.
# n9.0.1 is an ANNOTATED tag: `git ls-remote --tags` returns the TAG OBJECT (501bb494), not the commit.
# Resolved with `gh api repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/n9.0.1 --jq .sha`. Same trap as #395, which left a tag
# object in sources/mise.manifest's commit field for 17 days. Armed 2026-08-25: of the six tag-pinned
# sources added in this batch only FFmpeg ships annotated tags, so the probe discriminates.
url = https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
ref = n9.0.1
commit = bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa
kind = code
build = defer
defer_reason = #491: graphify detect exceeds its per-source deadline on FFmpeg's tree. A timeout, not an unclassified-file class, so #397's classifier widening does not reach it and the last round settled #491 as defers-not-closes. Clears when the per-source deadline is raised or detection is made incremental -- not by a manifest edit.
